SUMMARY:UC OSPO All-Campus Virtual Meetup: Ten Years of Browser Nano Exten
 sions   Show and Tell
LOCATION:Online
DESCRIPTION:Join the UC OSPO Network for an all-campus virtual meetup feat
 uring Neal Fultz\, statistical consultant for UCLA Social Sciences\, as he
  reflects on ten years of developing browser extensions. His interest bega
 n following the Anthem data breach\, inspiring him to create a series of s
 ix nano extensions\, each under 100 lines of code and compatible with Fire
 fox and Chrome-based browsers.\n\nFultz will explore the motivations and d
 evelopment behind the extensions\, and how the browser extension ecosystem
  differs from other open source communities. A Show and Tell follows the p
 resentation.\n\nHosted by UCLA Library's Tim Dennis and Leigh Phan. Zoom m
 eeting managed by the UC OSPO Network.\n\nRegistration is required.\n\nVie
 w upcoming UC OSPO Network events.
